    "type": "question",
    "label": "26",
    "prompt": "The line $y=3x+c$ intersects the line $3x-2y=6$ at the point $(-4,-9)$. Find the value of $c$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$c=3$",
      "worked": "Substituting $x=-4$ and $y=-9$ into $y=3x+c$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-9&=3(-4)+c\\\\-9&=-12+c\\\\c&=3\\end{align*}$$\nThe point also satisfies the second line: $3(-4)-2(-9)=6$.",
